<title>USA: Chaparral says president to resign.</title>
<headline>Chaparral says president to resign.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chaparral Resources Inc said Wednesday that Chairman Howard Karren has assumed the duties of chief executive, succeeding Paul Hoovler, who is expected to resign.</p>
<p>The company said that Hoovler will remain a director and president on an interim basis. In the meantime, it said it is expected to negotiate a severance agreement with Hoovler within the next 30 days.</p>
<p>Chaparral is a oil and gas exploration and production company. It said the changes are taking place as it seeks to become an international company.</p>
</text>
